Done. Semantic hints are injected across all six screens of the "Ever After" wedding-planner app (`web_applications_hinted/WebTestBench_0004`), attribute-only changes plus two prop-threading extensions for id scoping.

## Screens & components annotated
- **Navbar** (all pages): logo, 5 desktop nav links, mobile drawer copies suffixed `.mobile`, hamburger as `toggle` with `open`/`closed` state controlling `nav.menu.mobile`.
- **Dashboard (Index)**: hero couple/countdown observables, "Get Started" action opening `home.details.dialog`, the dialog's 5 inputs + save/cancel, 4 stat observables (state keys `wedding.date/budget/guestCount` shared with the inputs that edit them), 3 quick-link navigations with saved-count observables, saved-checklists preview collection, favorites preview collection.
- **Venues / Vendors**: filter region, search input (+ conditional clear), filter-chip groups as foldable collections of toggles with `selected`/`not-selected` state and `data-semtag-controls` pointing at the grid, results count, empty-state observable, card grid as `collection`.
- **Favorites**: empty-state + browse navigations, per-section counts, two card collections.
- **Checklists**: category chips (`checklists.filters.item.<cat>` incl. `all`), card grid, per-card expand toggle, saved-status badge, progress observable, save action, and each expanded card's tasks as a nested collection of checkboxes (`checklists.tasks.<clId>.item.<taskId>`).
- **NotFound**: message observable + home navigation.

## Id namespaces
`nav.*`, `home.*`, `venues.*`, `vendors.*`, `favorites.*`, `checklists.*` (+ `checklists.tasks.*`), `notfound.*`. Targets: `dashboard/venues/vendors/favorites/checklists.page`.

## Shared-component handling (§8)
`VenueCard`/`VendorCard` gained an optional `semtagCollection` prop and `SearchAndFilter` gained `semtagPrefix`/`semtagControls`; each call site supplies its own namespace (`venues.grid` vs `favorites.venues`, etc.), and **no attribute is emitted when the prop is absent** — no behavior change, all UI primitives already spread props. All collection containers are verified DOM ancestors of their items; item keys are stable domain ids (`v1`, `vn2`, `cl1-1`, filter values), never indices. Desktop/mobile nav duplication is the only cross-layout case, handled with `.mobile`.

## Deliberately unhinted
Vendor specialty badges, footer, decorative icons/images, layout wrappers, and the setup-less hero heading (so `home.hero.couple` stays statically unique).

